<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Weizi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">11th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century-bce">11th century BCE</a> · Also known as Weizi Qi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Weizi Qi was an elder brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/di-xin">Di Xin</a>, the last king of the Shang dynasty. After the failed rebellion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wu-geng">Wu Geng</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duke-of-zhou">Duke of Zhou</a> installed him at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shangqiu">Shangqiu</a> as ruler of the new state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a>, so that the sacrifices to the Shang royal ancestors would continue.</p></div>
